WEBVTT

00:09:28.287 --> 00:09:30.912
that their families were able
to give them nice burials,

00:09:30.954 --> 00:09:32.662
maybe even expensive ones.

00:09:32.704 --> 00:09:34.454
So even if we can't say their names,

00:09:34.496 --> 00:09:36.912
we can at least tell something
of their stories.

00:09:37.579 --> 00:09:39.746
And migration is part of my story, too.

00:09:39.787 --> 00:09:41.412
My grandparents came from Germany.

00:09:41.454 --> 00:09:44.621
My grandpa in 1923, to join his uncle.

00:09:44.662 --> 00:09:46.287
And my grandma a few years later.

00:09:46.329 --> 00:09:48.121
We just found their travel documents

00:09:48.162 --> 00:09:50.329
and a picture of my grandma
on a lounge chair

00:09:50.371 --> 00:09:53.829
on one of the big ships
that sailed across the Atlantic.

00:09:53.871 --> 00:09:56.412
We actually don't know
exactly why they came,

00:09:56.454 --> 00:09:58.329
but I imagine it's for the same reason

00:09:58.371 --> 00:10:00.746
that people come today
to the United States: